out.push(note('⚠ The last row is an honest ✗ and a small one; **part 3 being slightly longer than part 5 is a style note and not a fault.** ⚠ The fault the proportion rule exists to catch is the report where part 3 runs to three paragraphs and part 5 to one line — and that is the one to send back.'));
out.push(stage('6R', 'Share'));
out.push(p('Part 5 alone. ⚠ **Ask which change will happen and which will not, and why** — and the class predicts accurately: **the ones with a date and somebody waiting happen; the ones owned by the author with no external pressure do not.** That is the finding to act on.'));
out.push(stage('7', 'Write freely – sample (171 words)'));
out.push(sample(null, [
  'The best-written document I have seen about something going wrong was four pages about a fire door.',
  'It had what happened, in a timeline to the minute. It had what it cost, with a figure. And it had about two and a half pages of why, which were genuinely interesting: the door had been wedged open since a delivery in 2019, the wedge had been replaced twice by different people, and nobody had ever decided that the door should be open — it had simply become open.',
  'What it did not have was any line naming a person and a date. The final paragraph said that the importance of fire doors would be reinforced at the next safety briefing.',
  '⚠ **The door was still wedged open eighteen months later**, and the report was in a folder about nine metres from the door.',
  'What happened next was nothing, twice: ⚠ **the same report was written again after the next inspection, by somebody who had not read the first one**, and it reached the same conclusion with a different timeline.',
  '⚠ **Two excellent reports and one wedge.**',
]));
out.push(stage('7P', 'Respond – sample slip'));
out.push(p('★ _I am reading this as_ — "the inspector who will come next year"   ✓ _did the report have part 5?_ — "no — a briefing instead"   ? _which change had no owner, and is it still undone?_ — "all of them; the wedge is still there"'));
out.push(stage('7R', 'Share – sample'));
out.push(p('Usually the report lacked part 5 in all three texts, ⚠ **and in all three the event has happened again at least once.** ⚠ *Two excellent reports and one wedge* is the line to end the stage on: **the quality of the analysis has no relationship to whether anything changes, and the fifth part is the entire difference.**'));
out.push(stage('HW', 'Homework – sample (≈62 words)'));
out.push(sample(null, ['The fifth part of the fire-door report, written now: (a) **remove the wedge and fit a hold-open device with a magnetic release — the maintenance contractor, by the 28th, because it needs a certificate.** (b) **Record the door on the monthly walk-round — H. Mourad, from March, because she does it anyway.** ⚠ Two lines, two names, two dates, against two and a half pages of why.']));

// ===================== 15.7 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('15.7  Review & Mediate: what went wrong, and what we would do differently'));
out.push(stage('1', 'Get ready – Unit 15 quiz'));
out.push(p('**1** ⚠ ***I should have done the thing I was supposed to do*** (an apology, changes nothing) and ⚠ ***I should have written the line differently*** (a decision, can be unmade). **The second fixes a page.**  **2** ⚠ **Do we know what the other road looked like?** and ⚠ **did I take the decision?** — otherwise it is anger on paper, or an accusation.  **3** ⚠ **That the consequence is still true** — past and past is finished; past and present is an outstanding item, and the present half is where the figure goes.  **4** **What happened · what has changed · something the reader can forward** — ⚠ **and *sorry* is only one of them.**  **5** ⚠ **Was it in my power at the time?** — and ⚠ **look in the file first** when the wish is about somebody else.'));
out.push(stage('2', 'Listen and read'));
out.push(p('**a**  B   **b**  1 ⚠ **Telephone Ms Tannous on the 13th and not on the 15th** — she had a day and a half of knowing something was wrong and not knowing what, and nothing to tell her own customer.  2 Because she ⚠ **could not think how to write it as a line** — *telephone sooner* is an instruction to be better — and ⚠ **because she did not want to write *I delayed a day to look competent*, which is the true version.**'));
out.push(note('⚠ The exchange contains the hardest sentence in Book 2 so far and it must not be softened: ⚠ *I wanted to telephone her with the whole answer rather than with the question, and the whole answer was worth less to her than a day and a half of knowing.* **The delay was chosen, for a reason about appearance, and it cost the customer more than the nine cartons did.**'));
out.push(p('**Language box – Practise (sample):**  _"What is not in the report? If it started again next week, what would you do differently — and not one of the four changes? When did you know, as against when it was found? And can you write that as a rule rather than as an instruction to be better?"_'));
out.push(stage('3', 'Practise – sample with pair 2'));
out.push(dlg(null, [
  ['B', 'What is not in the report?'],
  ['A', 'Nothing. It is all there.'],
  ['B', 'If it started again next week, what would you do differently?'],
  ['A', 'I would put the telephone number on the note.'],
  ['B', '⚠ That is change (a). Something that is not one of the three.'],
  ['A', '…I would have turned round and come back rather than guessing, and lost two hours instead of a day.'],
  ['B', 'Why is that not in the report?'],
  ['A', '⚠ Because it sounds like *I should have been more sensible*. ⚠ But as a rule it is writable: **if an address is ambiguous and nobody answers, return; do not choose.**'],
]));
out.push(note('⚠ Pair 2 shows the mechanics exactly: the first answer is always a change already in the report, ⚠ **and B must refuse it and ask again.** The second answer is nearly always about a **decision the author made in the moment** — a delay, a guess, a telephone call not made — and that is the class of finding a self-written post-mortem cannot reach.'));
out.push(stage('3R', 'Perform'));
out.push(p('Listeners write the change that was not in the report and who found it. **Typical errors:** accepting the first answer · *telephone sooner* and *be more careful* offered as changes (⚠ **an instruction is not a change; a rule with a test in it is**) · and the content error, which is omitting who found it. ⚠ **A post-mortem that hides who found the finding teaches nobody to look** — and in this unit the finder had been in the job three weeks.'));
out.push(stage('4', 'Your turn – sample table'));
out.push(table(['The four questions', 'What they answered'], [
  ['What is not in the report', '"nothing" — then, on being asked again, the delay'],
  ['What they would do differently, not already a change', 'return rather than guess when an address is ambiguous'],
  ['When they knew, as against when it was found', '⚠ **knew at 16.20 on the road; the office knew at 08.30 the next day**'],
  ['⚠ The rule that replaces *be better*', '⚠ **if an address is ambiguous and nobody answers, return; do not choose.**'],
], [2.4, 3.6]));
out.push(stage('4R', 'Report – mediation'));
out.push(sample('Sample mediation', [
  '"The report has four changes, all about stencils and codes. The one that is not in it is: telephone the customer the same day I know, even with nothing to tell them. It is not in it because *telephone sooner* is not a change, and because the true version is that I delayed a day to look competent."',
  '⚠ **The unit\'s mediation, named as the third unit of this book:** a post-mortem is written by the person who caused the thing, **so it covers everything they can see and stops exactly where their own conduct begins** — and the change that cost the other side most is almost always about a delay the author chose, for a reason they are not proud of. ⚠ **Which means it will be found by somebody junior, or by nobody at all.**',
  '⚠ And the half that decides what to do: **the finding belongs to the question and not to the person who asked it.** Nour puts the change in with her own name against it and Lina\'s initials beside it as the finder — ⚠ **because a person whose finding is credited asks again in February, and a person who is thanked and not credited does not.**',
]));
out.push(stage('5', 'Read – exam practice (Reading Part 1)'));
out.push(table(['Q', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5'], [['Answer', 'A', 'B', 'B', 'B', 'B']], [1, 0.9, 0.9, 0.9, 0.9, 0.9]));
out.push(note('⚠ Q2 is the discriminating item and it is the unit in one question: the note is initialled **and** carries the list of objects affected, so the person has ⚠ **read it and written down what it affects.** A learner who answers **A** has read the initial as the whole of the record — ⚠ **which is exactly the error that produced the nine cartons**, and it is worth saying so when going over the answers.'));
out.push(note('⚠ Q5 is **B** and it rewards four words of close reading: *the stencils carry the code on the order* tests correctness, where *the stencils are on the bench* tested presence. ⚠ Q3 is **B**, not A: *K. Ayoub to decide* assigns a **decision**, and nothing on the line says he caused anything — **a learner who reads an owner as a culprit will misread every fifth part they ever see.**'));
out.push(stage('6', 'Write with help – sample (43 words)'));
out.push(sample('Exam task — Writing Part 1 (35 to 45 words)', [
  'Lina — change (c) from the post-mortem is yours: a one-page list of every object in the company that carries the consignee code — stencils, stamps, pre-printed labels, the office template. By Friday the 24th. Why you: because you do not know enough to leave anything off. If you find a fifth kind of object, tell me, not the warehouse.',
]));
out.push(note('⚠ That sample is 57 words and must be cut to forty-five. ⚠ The cut is the list of examples — *stencils, stamps, pre-printed labels, the office template* — because **the owner will find those herself and the point of the note is the ownership, the date and the reason.** ⚠ A learner who cuts the *why you* clause instead has removed the nine words that get the job done properly, and that is the commonest error in this task.'));
out.push(stage('6P', 'Check together – sample completed checklist'));
out.push(table(['Checklist', '✓ / ✗'], [
  ['The change, as a line that could go on a wall', '✓'],
  ['A date', '✓ Friday the 24th'],
  ['⚠ Why them, in one clause', '✓'],
  ['35 to 45 words — count them', '✗ 57 at the first attempt'],
], [5, 1]));
out.push(stage('7', 'Write freely – sample (176 words)'));
out.push(sample(null, [
  '**POST-MORTEM — THE DOUBLE-BOOKED THURSDAY. 5 February. H. Mourad. ⚠ One page.**',
  '**1 What happened.** Two customers were given the same 10.00 collection slot on Thursday 30 January. The first collected at 10.05. **The second waited fifty minutes outside a shut trade counter in the rain** and left without his goods.',
  '**2 What it cost.** His: **fifty minutes and a wasted journey from Jaramana.** Ours: **about an hour of mine, and he has not telephoned since.** ⚠ **Against the cost of printing a day page with the slots as lines — about twenty minutes, once.**',
  '**3 Why.** The collection book has an open page for each day, so a taken slot does not look taken. The contributing decision was mine: I kept an open page because it is quicker to write in. ⚠ **This is not a failure of attention — the page looked empty because it is always empty.**',
  '⚠ **4 What changes.** (a) A printed day page with the slots as lines. (b) The customer\'s telephone number written in the slot, not in my own book. (c) ⚠ **Nobody gives a slot without reading the line back aloud.**',
  '⚠ **5 Who owns each change.** (a) **H. Mourad, 6 February — done, printed.** (b) **H. Mourad, 6 February — done.** (c) ⚠ **L. Barakat and H. Mourad, from the 6th — because she is the newest and will do it audibly, which is how the rest of us will learn to.**',
  '⚠ **And the change that is about me and not about the book.** (d) **I telephoned the second customer on the Monday, not the Thursday.** H. Mourad, from now: ⚠ **telephone the same day, even with nothing to say but that I know.**',
]));
out.push(stage('HW', 'Homework – sample (≈64 words)'));
out.push(sample(null, ['I asked Lina what was not in my report. Her first answer was change (a), which is in it. ⚠ Her second: **that I give slots while I am on the telephone to somebody else, so I am never looking at the page when I write in it.** ⚠ **That is four years of my own habit, found in three weeks, and it is now change (e) with her initials against it.**']));

// ===================== UNIT CHECK =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(stage('✓', 'Unit 15 check – answers and marking'));
out.push(p('**A  Language** (8 marks — one each)'));
out.push(table(['Q', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8'], [['Answer', 'b', 'a', 'b', 'b', 'c', 'b', 'a', 'b']], [1, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7, 0.7]));
out.push(note('⚠ Questions 3 and 4 are the conditional pair and must be marked together: 3 is past-and-past (*would have gone*) and 4 is past-and-present (*would have*). ⚠ **A learner who gets 3 and misses 4 can describe what happened and cannot name what is still outstanding**, which is the difference between the two cycles.'));
out.push(note('⚠ Question 7 is the one to re-teach if missed: before writing *I wish somebody had told me*, ⚠ **look in the file.** In this unit the file contained a dated note with the writer\'s own initials on it — and a file is read by people who are looking for exactly that.'));
out.push(p('**B  Listening** (5 marks — one each)'));
out.push(table(['The change not in the report', 'When the writer knew', 'When the customer was telephoned', 'The honest reason', 'Who found it'], [[
  'telephone the customer the same day I know, even with nothing to tell them', 'about five on the 13th (the agent telephoned at four)', 'the 15th', '⚠ she wanted to telephone with the whole answer rather than the question', 'Lina',
]], [2, 1.5, 0.9, 2, 0.7]));
out.push(note('⚠ Gap 4 is the mark that separates a class that heard the exchange from one that understood it. ⚠ **Accept any wording that names *the whole answer* or *looking competent*; refuse *she was busy* and *she was finding out what happened***, which is what the delay looked like from outside and is not what the speaker said it was.'));
out.push(p('**C  Writing** (7 marks)'));
out.push(sample('Sample (68 words)', ['⚠ **4 What changes.** (a) A telephone-number column on the delivery note. (b) The office telephone diverts after four. (c) A list of the places on our routes with duplicate names.   ⚠ **5 Who owns each change.** (a) **H. Mourad, 10 February — done.** (b) **H. Mourad, 12 February.** (c) ⚠ **F. Saeed and the two other drivers, 20 February — because we are the only people who know which names repeat.**']));
out.push(box('Marking the Unit 15 check (20 marks)', [
  table(['', 'Marks', 'What earns them'], [
    ['**A Language**', '8', 'One per question. No half marks.'],
    ['**B Listening**', '5', 'One per gap; gap 4 needs the appearance reason, not *she was busy*.'],
    ['**C Writing**', '7', 'Lettered changes (1) · each change a line that could go on a wall (2) · ⚠ **a name for every change** (1) · ⚠ **a date for every change** (1) · a reason for at least one owner (1) · at least one change marked *done* (1).'],
  ], [1.2, 0.7, 4]),
  '⚠ **The two marks for *a line that could go on a wall* are the unit.** *We will be more careful* and *staff will be reminded* score 0 of those 2, however neatly lettered — ⚠ **because the test of a change is whether somebody who was not in the room could carry it out from the words alone.**',
  '⚠ **Give the date mark only if every change has one.** ⚠ **A change you own with no date is the commonest way a post-mortem dies**, and a part 5 with three dates and one blank will be done three-quarters of the way.',
  '⚠ **Deduct nothing for a short part 5 and deduct for a long part 3.** Three changes with names and dates beat seven with four blanks, ⚠ **and a *why* section longer than the fifth part is an essay about the writer however well it reads.**',
], C.lyellow, C.orange));
out.push(p('**Teacher\'s note — the three faults to watch in Unit 15**'));
out.push(p('**1 The emotional temperature, in both directions.** A unit about things going wrong produces either defensiveness or a competition in self-reproach, and both end the learning. ⚠ The single question that governs the whole unit is: ⚠ **can somebody who was not there act on this sentence tomorrow?** *I should have been more careful* fails it; *I should have written the line as* carry the code on the order *passes it. ⚠ Say the question aloud in 15.1 and return to it in every cycle — **a class that has it will write documents, and a class that has not will write feelings and then stop writing.**'));
out.push(p('**2 Person-level findings, which will keep coming back.** From 15.2 onwards learners revert to *he should have noticed* and *they should have told us*, because those sentences are available, quick and socially normal. ⚠ Two instruments stop it: **the question *against what?*** — Abu Yasser performed the check he was given, correctly — and ⚠ **the file**, which in this unit contains a dated note with the writer\'s own initials on it. ⚠ **Insist on the file check before any finding about another person**, every time, and the habit will survive the unit.'));
out.push(p('**3 Treating 15.7 as a courtesy.** The four questions look like a gentle ending and they are the only part of the unit a self-written post-mortem cannot do. ⚠ If a lesson has to be cut, **cut 15.3 and keep 15.7** — the mixed conditional can be taught inside 15.2 in ten minutes, and *what is not in the report* cannot be taught except by being asked it. ⚠ And run pair 2 of 15.7 with the whole class watching: **the first answer is always a change already in the report, and the asker must refuse it and ask again.** ⚠ The second answer is where the money is, and it is always about a decision the author made in the moment.'));

module.exports = out;
if (require.main === module) L.build(out, process.argv[2], 'Proactive Business English B1 · Book 2 · Syria Edition · Unit 15 · Answer Key');
